# Local-only: superseded versions, UI experiments, unused source images.
# Nothing in here is deployed.
# `_local/*` (not `_local/`) on purpose — a directory-matching pattern
# blocks git from even descending into it, which silently defeats any
# `!` negation below no matter how it's written. The wildcard form ignores
# the same contents by default but still lets git walk in and check them.
_local/*
# Exception: the Apps Script backend sources. HANDOVER.md already documents
# votes-apps-script.gs as "kept in _local/" as if it were tracked — it
# wasn't (git ls-files confirmed zero files under _local/ before this line
# existed), meaning a fresh clone silently lost the only copy of a real,
# deployed backend's source. These are actual source code, not disposable
# experiments; they belong with everything else in _local/ that's just
# private, not with things that are genuinely safe to lose.
!_local/*.gs
# Exception: archived PHP source (Phase 4, deferred — see
# _local/_archive/phase4-deferred-api/README.md). Same reasoning as the
# .gs exception above — real source code kept for a deliberate future
# reason, not a disposable experiment. Scoped narrowly to this one
# subfolder — the rest of _local/_archive/ (old design experiments, etc.)
# stays untracked as before.
!_local/_archive/
_local/_archive/*
!_local/_archive/phase4-deferred-api/
!_local/_archive/phase4-deferred-api/**

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.log
node_modules/
.claude/

# backend — never commit secrets or user uploads
api/config.php
*.lock
.tmp-*
decisions.json

# Live data written by api/publish.php, not source code. This site
# auto-deploys on git activity — tracking these meant every deploy (or
# apparently a periodic sync independent of pushes) could revert a real
# publish back to whatever was last committed. Confirmed happening live
# 2026-08-26: a test publish wrote successfully, then vanished within
# the same session with no push in between. Same reasoning as
# decisions.json above, just discovered later because these three
# started as committed placeholder content instead of starting empty.
/resources.json
/contributors.json
/files/*
!/files/.htaccess
